sMetadataExtension": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "PD-Poland|Template Unknown (author)|Polish Himalayan Expedition (1939)", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "I Polska Wyprawa w Himalaje (1939). Miejsce oznaczone strza\u0142k\u0105, gdzie zesz\u0142a lawina, pod kt\u00f3r\u0105 zgin\u0119li Stefan Bernadzikiewicz i Adam Karpi\u0144ski", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "1939", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "Jakub Bujak: \"Polish Himalayan expedition\" (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://crispa.uw.edu.pl/object/files/21434\">https://crispa.uw.edu.pl/object/files/21434</a>)", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "Unknown author<span style=\"display: none;\">Unknown author</span>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "Public domain", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "UsageTerms": {"value": "Public domain", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "AttributionRequired": {"value": "false", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Copyrighted": {"value": "False", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Restrictions": {"value": "", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "License": {"value": "pd", "source": "commons-templates", "hidden": ""}}, "mime": "image/jpeg"}]}, "-4": {"ns": 6, "title": "File:Shelter in Milam.jpg", "missing": "", "known": "", "imagerepository": "shared", "imageinfo": [{"size": 2153719, "width": 2153, "height": 3062, "thumburl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Shelter_in_Milam.jpg/1920px-Shelter_in_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "thumbwidth": 1600, "thumbheight": 2276, "responsiveUrls": {"2": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c5/Shelter_in_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}, "thumbattribs": {"src": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Shelter_in_Milam.jpg/1920px-Shelter_in_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "decoding": "async", "loading": "lazy", "width": 1600, "height": 2276, "srcset": "//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c5/Shelter_in_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"}, "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c5/Shelter_in_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original", "descriptionurl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shelter_in_Milam.jpg", "descriptionshorturl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=144904627", "extmetadata": {"DateTime": {"value": "2024-02-02 06:07:30", "source": "mediawiki-metadata", "hidden": ""}, "ObjectName": {"value": "Shelter in Milam", "source": "mediawiki-metadata"}, "CommonsMetadataExtension": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "Uttarakhand|Author died more than 70 years ago public domain images|PD US expired|CC-PD-Mark|PD-old missing SDC copyright status|PD-US missing SDC copyright status", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "(Translated from German via Google Translate) The Shepherd's place Milam is located close to where the Gori flows out of the Milam glacier at 3431 m (11250'). The inhabitants of the Gorithales who come here from June to September 81) (from Munsyari) belong to the mixed race of the Bhot-Rajputs, are proud, lazy, and very freedom-loving; It is not appropriate to act bossily towards them. Due to the barter trade with Tibet carried out in Milam, there is great prosperity; the Tibetans bring salt and soda from their salt lakes over the glaciated border passes on thousands of pack sheep and goats; such a sheep load ofsalt weighs about 30 pounds (approx. 15 kilos); You exchange 2 parts by weight of salt for 3 parts of barley, 7-8 parts of salt for 1 part of butter.\nIn Milam there is no \"bungalow\", but the Europeans who come here are given the facilities shown on plate XV (This image).", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "1894-12-25", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://pahar.in/\">https://pahar.in/</a>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "Kurt Boeck", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "Public domain", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "UsageTerms": {"value": "Public domain", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "AttributionRequired": {"value": "false", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Copyrighted": {"value": "False", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Restrictions": {"value": "", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "License": {"value": "pd", "source": "commons-templates", "hidden": ""}}, "mime": "image/jpeg"}]}, "-5": {"ns": 6, "title": "File:Nanda devi from a hill above Milam.jpg", "missing": "", "known": "", "imagerepository": "shared", "imageinfo": [{"size": 1750501, "width": 2004, "height": 2563, "thumburl": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Nanda_devi_from_a_hill_above_Milam.jpg/1920px-Nanda_devi_from_a_hill_above_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "thumbwidth": 1600, "thumbheight": 2046, "responsiveUrls": {"2": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Nanda_devi_from_a_hill_above_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}, "thumbattribs": {"src": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Nanda_devi_from_a_hill_above_Milam.jpg/1920px-Nanda_devi_from_a_hill_above_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail", "decoding": "async", "loading": "lazy", "width": 1600, "height": 2046, "srcset": "//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Nanda_devi_from_a_hill_above_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"}, "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Nanda_devi_from_a_hill_above_Milam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original", "descriptionurl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nanda_devi_from_a_hill_above_Milam.jpg", "descriptionshorturl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=144904628", "extmetadata": {"DateTime": {"value": "2024-02-02 06:07:30", "source": "mediawiki-metadata", "hidden": ""}, "ObjectName": {"value": "Nanda devi from a hill above Milam", "source": "mediawiki-metadata"}, "CommonsMetadataExtension": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "Nanda Devi|Author died more than 70 years ago public domain images|PD US expired|CC-PD-Mark|PD-old missing SDC copyright status|PD-US missing SDC copyright status", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "(Translated from German via Google Translate) The mountain ridge rising north behind Milam on the eastern edge of the Milam glacier is called Panchakuri. Its free location allows a comprehensive view of the high mountains of Kumaon. The legendary Nanda Devi appears most remarkable from its height in the southwest, whose 7,826 m (25,660') high rugged peak is connected to the very similarly shaped Nanda Kot by a vertical rock face; Keep in mind that the difference in height between the two peaks, which is so small in the picture, is no less than 390.7 m (1281'), as Nanda Kot is 7435.6 m (24379') high! This wonderful, enormous double peak is probably the most sublime mountain structure in the world.\n<p>According to the mountain dwellers, Siwa, the Hindu god intent on destruction, sits enthroned on this majestic mountain, together with his feared wife Kali or Parbati, whose surnames: Devi and Nanda gave the mountain a name that corresponds to its meaning: they only dare to venture with trembling and hesitation Native to the snow-covered parts of the mountains in order not to encounter this goddess of terror, whom they imagine as a black fury smeared with blood, with a hideous physiognomy, with a chain of human skulls around her neck and surrounded by poisonous snakes, while the god Siwa, adorned with human bones, is said to walk from mountain to mountain, intoxicated and roaring. Every stone fall, every avalanche is viewed as an expression of indignation by these deities, who are angry about the intrusion of humans into the sacred snowy area.\nIn the picture you can clearly see the separation of the ridges that project towards the Milam glacier, whose glaciers drain their water to the mighty wide outlet of the Milam glacier, visible below as a narrow silver thread.\n</p>\n(The author, I believe mislabeled Nanda Devi east as Nanda Kot, or the names were different back then.)", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "1894-12-25", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://pahar.in/\">https://pahar.in/</a>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "Kurt Boeck", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "Public domain", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "UsageTerms": {"value": "Public domain", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "AttributionRequired": {"value": "false", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Copyrighted": {"value": "False", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Restrictions": {"value": "", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "License": {"value": "pd", "source": "commons-templates", "hidden": ""}}, "mime": "image/jpeg"}]}}}}